it(\",\").map(Number)` reconstructs coordinates from strings — a fragile inverse of `toKey`. We can avoid the round-trip by storing the coordinate alongside the count, removing the parse step entirely (Rule 4 — fewer moving parts, and removes conceptual duplication of the key format between `toKey` and the split).\n\n### Step 2: Initial APP Mass (per-line, focusing on `nextGeneration`)\n\n**Final loop block (the refactoring target):**\n```\nfor (const [cellKey, count] of liveNeighborCounts) {   // loop 5, bindings cellKey+count = 2\n  const isAlive = liveCells.has(cellKey);               // binding 1, invocation .has 2, binding cellKey 1\n  if (count === 3 || (isAlive && count === 2)) {        // conditional 4, === x2 (2 inv=4), && (2), || (2), consts 3,2 (2), bindings count x2 + isAlive (3)\n    const [x, y] = cellKey.split(\",\").map(Number);      // bindings x,y 2, invocations split+map 4, const \",\" 1, binding Number+cellKey 2\n    result.push([x, y]);                                 // invocation push 2, bindings x,y 2\n  }\n}\n```\nLoop-block subtotal: 5 + 2 + (1+2+1) + (4+4+2+2+2+3) + (2+4+1+2) + (2+2) = **43**\n\n### Step 3–4: Apply Rule 2 (reveal intent) + Rule 4 (fewer elements)\n\nStore the coordinate with the count (avoids the string round-trip), and name the rule."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_016mNwsKrm2z2TGQGho4a5yW","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_06-03-04_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_opus-4-8/src/game-of-life.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const toKey = (x: number, y: number): string => `${x},${y}`;\n\nexport function nextGeneration(cells: Cell[]): Cell[] {\n  const liveCells = new Set<string>(cells.map(([x, y]) => toKey(x, y)));\n\n  const liveNeighborCounts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const [x, y] of cells) {\n    for (const [dx, dy] of NEIGHBOR_OFFSETS) {\n      const neighborKey = toKey(x + dx, y + dy);\n      liveNeighborCounts.set(neighborKey, (liveNeighborCounts.get(neighborKey) ?? 0) + 1);\n    }\n  }\n\n  const result: Cell[] = [];\n  for (const [cellKey, count] of liveNeighborCounts) {\n    const isAlive = liveCells.has(cellKey);\n    if (count === 3 || (isAlive && count === 2)) {\n      const [x, y] = cellKey.split(\",\").map(Number);\n      result.push([x, y]);\n    }\n  }\n  return result;\n}","newText":"const toKey = (x: number, y: number): string => `${x},${y}`;\n\nconst survivesOrIsBorn = (isAlive: boolean, liveNeighbors: number): boolean =>\n  liveNeighbors === 3 || (isAlive && liveNeighbors === 2);\n\nexport function nextGeneration(cells: Cell[]): Cell[] {\n  const liveCells = new Set<string>(cells.map(([x, y]) => toKey(x, y)));\n\n  const neighborCounts = new Map<string, { cell: Cell; count: number }>();\n  for (const [x, y] of cells) {\n    for (const [dx, dy] of NEIGHBOR_OFFSETS) {\n      const cell: Cell = [x + dx, y + dy];\n      const key = toKey(cell[0], cell[1]);\n      const existing = neighborCounts.get(key);\n      neighborCounts.set(key, { cell, count: (existing?.count ?? 0) + 1 });\n    }\n  }\n\n  const result: Cell[] = [];\n  for (const [key, { cell, count }] of neighborCounts) {\n    if (survivesOrIsBorn(liveCells.has(key), count)) {\n      result.push(cell);\n    }\n  }\n  return result;\n}"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":2609,"output":2814,"cacheRead":10356,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":15779,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784959654814,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-0abb2405-e0fe-4817-a670-85de1930e995","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_016mNwsKrm2z2TGQGho4a5yW","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_06-03-04_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_opus-4-8/src/game-of-lif